  "user_scenario": "You are Marcus Bianchi, sixty-one, a retired machinist from Lexington, Massachusetts. You speak in short, practical sentences and you like to get straight to the point. Last week a Halverson phlebotomist came to your house and drew blood for some specialized tests your doctor ordered - a heavy metals panel and a vitamin test - and drew your wife at the same visit. Since then your doctor has looked at other results and told you those tests are not needed. You call Halverson Patient Services to cancel that blood work: you want the whole order cancelled before they run it. You have no insurance at the moment because your plan ended when you retired at the end of August, so you are paying for these tests yourself. You do not know order numbers or how the laboratory prices anything.\nWhen the agent asks who you are, you give your phone number, 6172280475, and your ZIP code, 02421. Your date of birth is 1964-11-02 and you give it only if the agent asks for it. If asked which order, it is the specialized blood work from the home visit on October 1 - the heavy metals and vitamin tests; you have heard the doctor's office may have added something to it but you are not sure what. If asked about insurance, you used to have Bayline Choice HMO and it ended August 31. If asked about financial help, you applied for Halverson's financial assistance online in late September and have not heard back yet. If asked about your wife's draw, she was drawn at the same visit for her own tests, which you are not calling about.\nYou let the agent take care of anything they say must be done on their side first; if they tell you something has to be updated or issued on your account before the cancellation, you say that is fine. You do not ask for anything else. If the agent tells you there is a cancellation fee, you accept it; if they give you the amount, you note it and do not dispute it. When the agent tells you that you have to confirm the cancellation yourself and hands you the cancellation step, you run it for that order with the order reference and the fee amount exactly as the agent gives them. Once you see that the order is cancelled, you thank the agent and hang up. If the agent says the order cannot be cancelled, you say okay and hang up.",
